meta {
  name: Create Temporary Document Type
  type: http
  seq: 16
}

post {
  url: {{CRM_URL}}/rpa_documenttypeses
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

script:pre-request {
  // Defined here, not in a vars:pre-request block. bru.getVar reads only
  // runtime variables; a vars:pre-request entry populates request variables,
  // which are a separate collection used solely for {{...}} interpolation and
  // are invisible to bru.getVar. Override with a TEMP_DOCUMENT_TYPE
  // environment variable if a different name is wanted.
  const documentType = bru.getEnvVar("TEMP_DOCUMENT_TYPE") || "FLS1-169-no-such-doc-type";

  // rpa_name is capped at 13 characters on this entity, which is why the real
  // rows carry short codes such as DUAPPEVD rather than the document type
  // name. It is a separate value from rpa_documenttype, which is the
  // attribute the case-type lookup actually filters on and is not so capped.
  const NAME_MAX_LENGTH = 13;
  const name = bru.getEnvVar("TEMP_DOCUMENT_TYPE_NAME") || "FLS1169TMP";
  if (name.length > NAME_MAX_LENGTH) {
    throw new Error(`rpa_name "${name}" is ${name.length} characters; the entity allows ${NAME_MAX_LENGTH}.`);
  }

  const navs = {
    scheme: bru.getEnvVar("SCHEME_NAV"),
    subject: bru.getEnvVar("SUBJECT_NAV"),
    teamRouting: bru.getEnvVar("TEAMROUTING_NAV")
  };
  const values = {
    scheme: bru.getEnvVar("SCHEME_VALUE"),
    subject: bru.getEnvVar("SUBJECT_VALUE"),
    teamRouting: bru.getEnvVar("teamRoutingValue")
  };

  // documentType is checked alongside the rest. JSON.stringify drops a key
  // whose value is undefined, so an unset name does not fail the request: it
  // creates a nameless row that the case-type lookup can never match, and the
  // replay goes on reporting document_type_not_found with nothing to show why.
  const missing = Object.entries({ ...navs, ...values, documentType, name })
    .filter(([, v]) => !v)
    .map(([k]) => k);
  if (missing.length) {
    throw new Error(`Missing ${missing.join(", ")}. Run "Get Document Type Lookup Bind Names" for the nav properties and "Get Document Type Metadata" against a working type for the values.`);
  }

  const payload = {
    rpa_documenttype: documentType,
    rpa_name: name
  };
  payload[`${navs.scheme}@odata.bind`] = `/rpa_schemes(${values.scheme})`;
  payload[`${navs.subject}@odata.bind`] = `/subjects(${values.subject})`;
  payload[`${navs.teamRouting}@odata.bind`] = `/teams(${values.teamRouting})`;

  console.log(JSON.stringify(payload, null, 2));
  bru.setVar("tempDocumentTypeBody", JSON.stringify(payload));
}

body:json {
  {{tempDocumentTypeBody}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Prefer: return=representation
}

script:post-response {
  const body = res.getBody();
  const id = body?.rpa_documenttypesid;
  if (id) {
    bru.setEnvVar("TEMP_DOCUMENT_TYPE_ID", id);
    console.log(`created "${body.rpa_documenttype}" as ${id}`);
    if (!body.rpa_documenttype) {
      console.log('WARNING: the row has no rpa_documenttype. The case-type lookup filters on that attribute alone, so nothing will ever match it. Delete the row and investigate.');
    }
    console.log('Delete it with "Delete Temporary Document Type" once the evidence is captured.');
  } else {
    console.log(`HTTP ${res.getStatus()}`);
    console.log(JSON.stringify(body, null, 2));
  }
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Creates a throwaway rpa_documenttypeses row, so that a submission which
  failed with document_type_not_found can be replayed and succeed. That is
  FLS1-169 acceptance criterion 7: a message replays cleanly once the
  underlying CRM data is corrected.

  A throwaway row is used in preference to repairing a real one. The only
  genuinely incomplete row in rpadevv9 is CS_Capital_Claim_Evidence, which is
  missing its team routing, and the correct team for it must come from DDTS
  CRM. Guessing would write wrong routing into live reference data, and a real
  submission arriving during the window would then be created against the
  wrong team, which is worse than the failure it replaces.

  h4. Before running

  # "Get Document Type Lookup Bind Names" sets SCHEME_NAV, SUBJECT_NAV and
    TEAMROUTING_NAV.
  # "Get Document Type Metadata" against a working type, Appeal_Evidence for
    instance, sets SCHEME_VALUE, SUBJECT_VALUE and teamRoutingValue.

  The pre-request script builds the payload from those six values and refuses
  to run if any is missing. The bind paths assume the lookups target
  rpa_schemes, subjects and teams, confirmed against rpadevv9 by
  "Get Document Type Lookup Bind Names".

  h4. Two attributes, not one

  rpa_documenttype is what getDocumentTypeMetadata filters on, so it carries
  the full case type such as FLS1-169-no-such-doc-type. rpa_name is a
  *separate* short code, capped at 13 characters, which is why the real rows
  hold values like DUAPPEVD. Setting rpa_name to the full case type is
  rejected with "The length of the 'rpa_name' attribute ... exceeded the
  maximum allowed length of '13'". The script defaults it to FLS1169TMP;
  override with TEMP_DOCUMENT_TYPE_NAME.

  h4. Afterwards

  *Delete the row.* It is test data in a shared organisation, and while it
  exists the case type is a valid choice that routes to whichever team was
  copied. TEMP_DOCUMENT_TYPE_ID is set for "Delete Temporary Document Type".

  The case created by the replay is also junk. Ask DDTS CRM whether they want
  it deactivated.

  h4. If this answers 403

  The application user may be permitted to write cases and triage records but
  not reference data. In that event acceptance criterion 7 needs DDTS CRM to
  make the change, and cannot be completed from here.
}
